<% layout('layout/boilerplate.ejs') %>

<main>
  <section class="section container">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">&larr; Back</a>

    <div class="feature-card">
      <div class="feature-card-header">
        <span class="feature-card-dot"></span>
        <span class="feature-card-dot"></span>
        <span class="feature-card-dot"></span>
        <span class="title">portal — voult.dev</span>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card-body">
        <div class="feature-full">
          <h1>Rich developer portal</h1>
          <p class="feature-full-intro">
            Launching auth is just the beginning. Keeping it healthy requires visibility. Our dashboard and CLI give you the data you need without the engineering overhead.
          </p>

          <h2>What's included</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Interactive dashboard</strong> — sign-up rates, login success rates, and user growth at a glance. Filter by date range or provider.</li>
            <li><strong>Live metrics</strong> — failed login attempts, token refresh frequency, and session duration trends. Spot anomalies before they become incidents.</li>
            <li><strong>OAuth provider breakdown</strong> — see which providers (Google, GitHub, etc.) are driving sign-ups and where users drop off.</li>
            <li><strong>CLI access</strong> — run <code>voult metrics</code> from your terminal to pull the same data into your own tooling or CI checks.</li>
            <li><strong>Audit logs</strong> — every authentication event is logged. Search, filter, and export for compliance or debugging purposes.</li>
          </ul>

          <p>
            Authentication is silent infrastructure. When it works, nobody notices. The portal is there for the times when they do—and so you can measure how well it's working.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>
